---
// No props — static content
---

<div
  style="background-color:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;"
>
    <div style="padding:1rem 1.25rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;">
      <span
        style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text);"
      >
        The Method
      </span>
      <span class="badge" style="background:rgb(79 142 247/0.12);color:#4f8ef7;border:1px solid rgb(79 142 247/0.25);">
        Recalibrated
      </span>
    </div>

  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);padding:1.25rem;">
    <!-- The Rule -->
    <div style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
      <p class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">The Rule</p>
      <div
        style="background-color:var(--color-surface-2);border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:6px;padding:0.875rem 1rem;font-size:0.86rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--color-text);"
      >
        <strong>Mismatch</strong> = back the win, be bold on the margin. 3-0 or 4-0, not a timid 2-0.
        <strong>Even game</strong> = the draw is the default. Back a winner only with a named edge.
        Always name the talisman. Attach a confidence % to every call, anchored on the market.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Lessons -->
    <div>
      <p class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Lessons from the data</p>
      <ol
        style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.5rem;"
      >
        {[
          ['Outcome calls', '6 of 7 result misses were "backed a winner, game drew." The quality read was usually right. The opener regime was not. Fix: treat the draw as the base case in even games.'],
          ['Opener draw rate', '37% draw rate in MD1 vs ~28% baseline. Openers are uniquely cautious: teams take a point over a risky win. Draw rate should fall from MD2 onward. Do not overfit to the opener pattern.'],
          ['Scorer calls', 'The engine\'s biggest strength at ~67%. Keep naming the talisman. The commitment forces clarity and this is where the engine earns consistently.'],
          ['Confidence anchoring', 'Every call now carries a % anchored on the market. Deviating from the market requires a named reason. The calibration chart on the dashboard is the feedback loop.'],
        ].map(([heading, text]) => (
          <li
            style="display:flex;gap:0.75rem;background-color:var(--color-surface-2);border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:6px;padding:0.65rem 0.875rem;font-size:0.83rem;line-height:1.6;"
          >
            <span style="color:var(--color-accent);font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;">{heading}:</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text);opacity:0.85;">{text}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
